; EXODUS.BIN: Ultima III (Origin 1983, PC version by James R. Van Artsdalen).
; Generated by tools/gen.py; tools/build.py builds it (MASM, LINK, then the image from 0100).
; EXDATA: map buffer, entry vector, tables and strings (0100-1BD5).
;
; The data at the start of EXODUS.BIN, used by every other module:
;  - 0080-00AC: not memory of EXODUS but offsets into the combat area (StartUp, 24C4), written
;    as labels in the PSP so that `CmbMonHP[si]` = StartUp + 98h + si (docs/FORMATS.md 5 and 9);
;  - 0100-1327 MapBuf: the map file (SOSARIA.ULT, AMBROSIA.ULT or a town, 1228h bytes; in a
;    dungeon DUNGEON.DAT and the dungeon file), FORMATS.md 3, 4, 8;
;  - 1328: the entry vector (BOOTUP jumps through it to StartUp); 132A ScreenRowTbl;
;  - 14BA-15CB: PARTY.ULT as loaded (the 18-byte header and four 64-byte records, FORMATS.md 6),
;    then the game's variables (position, light, dungeon level, ...) and file names;
;  - the surface command table (keys 1887, prompts 18C9, handlers 190B), the moon gates,
;    creature spawning tables and the strings of the surface commands (LOOP, WORLD);
;  - 1B77-1BD4: code: ReadCommand, the top of the surface turn (it continues in LOOP).
CODE SEGMENT BYTE PUBLIC
ASSUME CS:CODE, DS:CODE, ES:CODE, SS:CODE
EXTRN PutChar:NEAR
EXTRN KeyReady:NEAR
EXTRN ReadKey:NEAR
EXTRN CmdPass:NEAR
EXTRN CmdNorth:NEAR
EXTRN CmdSouth:NEAR
EXTRN CmdEast:NEAR
